      "claim": "The long-chain ether lipid ET-18-OCH3 showed clear blood-brain barrier penetration in rats with a brain uptake index of 10.7%, classified as good penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C14"],
      "claim": "Electrophilic nitro-oleic acid, a modified long-chain fatty acid, moves facilely across the rat BBB, indicating that polar/functionalized long-chain lipids can still achieve CNS entry.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "A radiolabeled triglyceride crossed the mouse BBB intact, showing that larger, complex lipid assemblies can achieve brain uptake.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple high-transfer experimental records demonstrate that long-chain fatty acids and complex lipids cross the BBB via uptake mechanisms despite unfavorable passive-diffusion properties. The query's long lipophilic chain and lipid-like scaffold align with this evidence, supporting meaningful CNS access.",
